{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550775-distinguished-palate-preferences","id":1550775,"title":"Distinguished Palate Preferences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-06T18:03:10-07:00","id":1550775,"title":"Distinguished Palate Preferences","content":"The 2e core book (pg. 111) describes preferences suitable for the drawback of Distinguished Palate as being &quot;no more than one-tenth of the population,&quot; and including as examples blood types, hair colors, and the presence of particular drugs. What other preferences have you seen be allowed within a chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T20:51:47-07:00","id":1550781,"title":"","content":"Specific ethnicities, family lines, members of certain religious denominations, urban tribes, professions? Many possible way to extrapolate from the base concept i'd guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T19:23:15-07:00","id":1550926,"title":"","content":"This Merit reminds me of the Ventrue weakness from the old <i>World of Darkness</i>. I\u2019d even go as far as to stretch it to different things, like a specific method of consuming blood. Don\u2019t lean too heavily on the 1-in-10 thing, because that can be really easy to metagame. I mean, there are 8 billion people in the world, and the USA alone has around 400 million, so pretty much every American could fit into that 1-in-10 rule.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d allow stranger criteria, like age brackets, people who committed a certain sin (lust being a common one) on that night, celibates (increasingly common these days), vegans, etc. As long as the player can justify it in a way that makes sense for their character. The idea is to tell a good story, not just to MinMax Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-10T20:10:32-07:00","id":1550929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1550775-distinguished-palate-preferences?p=1550926#post1550926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Merit reminds me of the Ventrue weakness from the old <i>World of Darkness</i>. I\u2019d even go as far as to stretch it to different things, like a specific method of consuming blood. Don\u2019t lean too heavily on the 1-in-10 thing, because that can be really easy to metagame. I mean, there are 8 billion people in the world, and the USA alone has around 400 million, so pretty much every American could fit into that 1-in-10 rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is 1-in-10 <i>at the broadest</i> if one requires a reference, with rarer, stranger criteria <b><i>being the expected norm</i></b> in fact.<br /> <br /> Just wished to clear that up, since it's how i understood things at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T05:46:14-07:00","id":1550938,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea is just to want to be able to tell an interesting story about the preference being there. These are good so far!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T19:48:14-07:00","id":1550981,"title":"","content":"The best guideline to think of a preference is to think what the character will do with it.<br /> <br /> Can the character create such things in some ways? Imagine a preference for people who've been hungry for 24h+, or for the victims of a certain crime. If it is a lineage of some sort, what the character does to surround themselves with this group, or even expand it with time? A drug or crime is also something the character can create in a pinch, but at what social and/or moral cost?<br /> <br /> What the character does, or is tempted to do, with the restriction is the main question to be addressed, and you should think/talk with the player about what aspect of the character is to be highlighted by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}